The policy defines a Hospital as a facility that:

- is registered under the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority (IRDA) Act 2010 or the enactments listed in Section 56(1) of that Act, or meets all of the following minimum criteria:
  – employs qualified nursing staff round-the-clock;
  – has at least 10 in-patient beds in towns with a population below 1 million, and at least 15 in-patient beds elsewhere;
  – has qualified medical practitioner(s) on duty round-the-clock;
  – possesses its own fully equipped operation theatre where surgical procedures are performed;
  – maintains daily patient records and makes them available to the insurer’s authorised personnel.
